# Open data live — WAQI air quality, GBFS bike share & baked OSM POIs

**Dev-only.** Open-data overlays: **WAQI** air stations and **GBFS** bike-share docks (Styr & Ställ / nextbike_zg) are fetched in the browser on demand; **OSM places** use a **baked JSON** file produced by `source/data/osm/export_osm_pois.py`. All are shown in dev overlay panels and mirrored as runtime USD geometry in Kit. Production streaming does **not** load this extension.

The **dev IoT drawer (`IotSubmenu.tsx`) hosts air quality, bike share, baked OSM places, and live transit (Västtrafik)** — using the same shape where applicable: a primary action, an "Open list" entry-point, and a status/error line. List panels (`IotAirStationsPanel`, `IotBikeSharePanel`, `IotOsmPoisPanel`, `IotTransitLivePanel`) let the user select a row to pan the bird-eye camera (or ground teleport) and show details. See `transit-live-overlay.mdc` for live vehicles; see **`osm-poi-overlay.mdc`** for OSM stops vs live buses.

## Kit extension

| Item | Location |
|------|----------|
| Extension | `younite.open_data_live_extension` (shared with live transit) |
| Lifecycle + events | `extension.py` (air + bike + OSM POIs + transit wiring) |
| Air geometry + highlight | `services/air_quality_stations.py` (`AirQualityStationsService`) |
| Bike geometry + highlight | `services/bike_share_service.py` (`BikeShareStationsService`, reuses pole/halo/beacon helpers from `air_quality_stations.py`) |
| OSM POI geometry + highlight | `services/osm_poi_markers_service.py` (`OsmPoiMarkersService`, pole/halo/beacon layout; vivid default crowns + selection accent — see `osm-poi-overlay.mdc`) |
| Shared focus helper | `_focus_lat_lon(lat, lon)` in `extension.py` — bird-eye pan via `birdEyePanFocusWorld`, else ground teleport. Reused by air + bike + OSM list selection. |
| Shared event wiring | `_register_station_service(...)` in `extension.py` — registers `{prefix}{Stations,Toggle,FocusStation,HighlightStation}`. Optional **`cache_stations_attr`** + **`after_stations_sync`** (used by OSM) for late georef + replay on **`scene.loaded`**. |
| Kit profile | `younite.usd_viewer_streaming_dev.kit` only (`order = 1205`) |

**Dependencies** (see `config/extension.toml`): messaging, payload orchestrator, `usd_viewer_stage_core` (GeoCoordinateService for WGS84 → USD), `osm_navigation` + `omni.physx` (for the bundled transit service), `omni.usd`.

**USD root (air)**: prims under `/World/IoT_AirQuality/Stations` (sublayer `iot_air_quality_layer.usda`). Each station is an Xform with pole, emissive “halo” sphere (AQI palette), and ground beacon. Neutral pole/beacon color; crown sphere color reflects AQI.

**USD root (bike)**: prims under `/World/IoT_BikeShare/Stations` (sublayer `iot_bike_share_layer.usda`). Same pole/beacon/halo layout; crown color reflects bike availability (empty = red, few = amber, several = green).

**USD root (OSM POIs)**: prims under `/World/IoT_OsmPois/Stations` (sublayer `iot_osm_pois_layer.usda`). Same layout; **category** is stored on prims for metadata — stream-visible colours are a shared high-contrast palette (see `osm-poi-overlay.mdc`).

**Custom data** on air station root (when provided by web): `iot:lat`, `iot:lon`, `iot:aqi`, `iot:name`, optional `iot:pm25`, `iot:temp_c`, `iot:time`.

**Custom data** on bike station root: `iot:lat`, `iot:lon`, `iot:name`, `iot:bikes`, `iot:docks`.

**Custom data** on OSM POI root: `iot:lat`, `iot:lon`, `iot:name`, `iot:category`, optional `iot:detail`, `iot:opening_hours`.

**Visibility**: geometry show/hide goes through `batch_show_hide` from the payload orchestrator (`SOURCE = "open_data_live"`), not raw `MakeVisible` / `MakeInvisible`.

**Stage lifecycle**: on `omni.usd@stage_event` OPENED/CLOSED, the service clears tracked station prims.

Startup failure is logged once with `[open_data_live] startup failed: …` (no per-frame spam).

