| Baked OSM JSON import | `src/services/iot/osmPoisBaked.ts` → `kit-app-template-main/source/data/osm/osm_pois_gbg.json` |
| Air types / Kit payload | `src/types/iotAirQuality.ts` |
| Bike types / Kit payload | `src/types/iotBikeShare.ts` |
| OSM POI types / categories | `src/types/iotOsmPois.ts` |
| Dev menu (fetch, open list) | `src/features/dev/controls/submenus/IotSubmenu.tsx` (drawer: AIQ + bike + OSM + live transit) |
| Live transit dev block (same IoT drawer) | `src/features/dev/controls/submenus/TransitLiveDevSection.tsx` |
| Air panel + AQI/temp scales | `src/features/streaming/overlays/iotAirQuality/` |
| Bike panel | `src/features/streaming/overlays/iotBikeShare/IotBikeSharePanel.tsx` (reuses air panel CSS) |
| OSM panel + category toggle | `src/features/streaming/overlays/iotOsmPois/IotOsmPoisPanel.tsx` (one category at a time → Kit markers) |
| Transit panel | `src/features/streaming/overlays/iotTransitLive/IotTransitLivePanel.tsx` (reuses air panel CSS) — see `transit-live-overlay.mdc` |
| **IoT list shell (mobile)** | `src/features/streaming/overlays/iotShared/` — `IotPanelLayout`, `useIotPanelDrag`, barrel `index.ts`; narrow viewports (≤639px): bottom sheet, capped height, drag handle to dismiss, safe-area padding. Styles live in `iotAirQuality/IotAirStationsPanel.css`. |
| Panel open state + dismiss | `useControlHandlers.ts` (dismiss helpers + IoT state for all panels) |
| Overlay mount | `SharedOverlayLayer.tsx` (mounts IoT panels) |

**Token**: `VITE_WAQI_TOKEN` in repo-root `.env` (Vite `envDir` is parent of `web-viewer-sample-main`); see `.env.example`.

**Bike feed**: default GBFS root `https://api.nextbike.net/maps/gbfs/v1/nextbike_zg/gbfs.json` — optional override `VITE_GBFS_BIKE_URL` in `.env`.

**Data**: map/bounds response supplies AQI and sometimes `iaqi` (PM2.5, temperature `t`). `enrichStationsMissingPm25` backfills per-station feed data for missing PM2.5 and/or `tempC` (WAQI `iaqi.t`). Station `id` uses `waqi_<uid>` when the API provides `uid`.

**UI**: dev-only English strings (not in customer i18n). Panel supports **AQI** vs **Temperature** toggle; temperature scale is a separate educational strip (−50 … +50 °C for marker position). **Web ↔ Kit ordering:** list panels send **`*Stations` before `*HighlightStation`** so Kit applies highlight to the current prim set (air, bike, OSM).

## Web ↔ Kit messaging

Registered in `extension.py` via `kit_app.register_event_alias` + `carb.eventdispatcher.observe_event`:

| Event | Direction | Purpose |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| `iotAirQualityStations` | Web → Kit | Payload `{ stations: IotAirQualityStation[] }`. **Empty list removes** all station prims (`sync_stations` → `clear`). |
| `iotAirQualityToggle` | Web → Kit | Payload `{ enabled: bool }` — toggles visibility of existing station geometry via orchestrator (optional; empty station list clears prims entirely). |
| `iotAirQualityFocusStation` | Web → Kit | `{ lat, lon }` — bird-eye: pan view center toward station base; else ground teleport. |
| `iotAirQualityHighlightStation` | Web → Kit | `{ id: string \| null }` — list selection highlight (emissive / halo emphasis). |
| `iotBikeShareStations` | Web → Kit | Payload `{ stations: IotBikeShareStation[] }`. **Empty list removes** all bike dock prims. |
| `iotBikeShareToggle` | Web → Kit | Payload `{ enabled: bool }` — toggles visibility of existing bike geometry via orchestrator. |
| `iotBikeShareFocusStation` | Web → Kit | `{ lat, lon }` — same focus/teleport behaviour as air. |
| `iotBikeShareHighlightStation` | Web → Kit | `{ id: string \| null }` — list selection highlight for bike markers. |
| `iotOsmPoisStations` | Web → Kit | `{ stations: [{ id, lat, lon, category }] }` — **active category**, slim rows only (no name/hours/detail); empty list clears OSM POI prims. |
| `iotOsmPoisToggle` | Web → Kit | `{ enabled: bool }` — visibility toggle via orchestrator. |
| `iotOsmPoisFocusStation` | Web → Kit | `{ lat, lon }` — same focus behaviour as air/bike. |
| `iotOsmPoisHighlightStation` | Web → Kit | `{ id: string \| null }` — selection highlight. |

**Markers only while the panel is open**: when a list panel opens, it sends the corresponding `*Stations` event with the current list. On close, the web sends `{ stations: [] }` and clears highlight. Refresh in the dev IoT submenu loads data and opens the bike panel when docks exist; reopening uses “Open docks list” without refetch until Refresh is pressed again. **OSM:** data is bundled from `osm_pois_gbg.json`; refresh the file by re-running `export_osm_pois.py`, then rebuild the web app if needed.

## World state sync

These markers are **ephemeral dev overlays**, not part of the production world snapshot. They are **not** registered on `WorldStateSyncService` today. If a future requirement needs reconnect persistence, design an explicit snapshot field with the team first.

